1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,050
From a training application in source control to a live deployment on Amazon EKS.

2
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:12,100
The frontend handles signup, login, and the roadmap page. Auth and Roadmap APIs serve it, while MySQL stores user accounts.

3
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:18,150
Docker Compose starts the frontend, APIs, and MySQL together with configured networking, environment values, and health checks.

4
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:24,200
Terraform provisions a VPC across two Availability Zones, public and private subnets, EKS, ECR, and encrypted S3 state.

5
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:30,250
GitHub Actions builds each service image on hosted runners and scans the images with Trivy before publishing.

6
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:36,300
Passing images are pushed to private ECR repositories with immutable commit tags. GitHub Actions updates the matching Kubernetes manifest in Git.

7
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:42,350
Argo CD watches the dev overlay in Git and continuously reconciles its Kubernetes resources into Amazon EKS.

8
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:48,400
The EKS cluster runs the frontend, Auth API, Roadmap API, and MySQL StatefulSet. The EBS CSI driver provisions the gp3 database volume.

9
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:54,450
The AWS Load Balancer Controller creates an Application Load Balancer. It routes browser traffic to the frontend, which calls the APIs inside the cluster.

10
00:00:54,450 --> 00:01:00,950
Terraform provisions AWS, GitHub Actions builds and scans images, and Argo CD syncs Git manifests into Kubernetes.
